module v2.lens.common.source_analysis_standing


// SourceUnreadable IS THE ARM THE PIPELINE HAD NO WAY TO REACH, and its absence was not a gap in
// coverage but an abort. Every consumer of this coproduct obtains its subject by reading a file,
// and the read ran through the `filesystem_read` intrinsic, whose result carries content and
// nothing else: a path that does not exist raises an interpreter type error and takes the WHOLE
// run down, so a roster or corpus sweep learned nothing about the files after the missing one.
// Receipt: src/v2/workflow/glob_discovery_law.dag moved to src/v2/test/workflow/ in the #9637
// directory reorganisation and the roster row that names it was not repointed; because the roster
// gate is offline, nothing ran it, and the row sat crashing rather than refusing until a
// corpus-grain consumer executed it (2026-09-06).
//
// The read now folds through extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io's filesystem_read_outcome, so an
// unreadable subject is one typed, located, counted row and the sweep continues.
type SourceAnalysisNotEstablishedCause
  = LanguageGrammarUnavailable
  | LanguageGrammarRejected
  | SourceUnreadable
  | SourceTokenizationRejected
  | SourceParseRejected
  | SourceNormalizationRejected

